var quick_start_default = "---\nlayout: article\ntitle: Quick start\ndescription: Choose an Appwrite partner integration model and take your first steps with OAuth connect or organization API keys.\n---\n\nThis quick start helps you pick the right integration path and wire up your first Console API call.\n\n# Choose your integration model {% #choose-your-integration-model %}\n\n| Model | Best for | Auth |\n| ----- | -------- | ---- |\n| [OAuth connect](/docs/partners/oauth-connect) | Users link existing Appwrite accounts | User consent via OAuth 2.0 |\n| [Org API keys](/docs/partners/org-api-keys) | Your platform provisions resources in your org | Organization API key |\n\nUse **OAuth connect** when your customers already use Appwrite and want to grant your product access to their organizations.\n\nUse **org API keys** when your platform creates and manages Appwrite projects, domains, and resources inside an organization you control.\n\n# Prerequisites {% #prerequisites %}\n\n- An Appwrite Cloud account with an organization\n- A server-side environment to store secrets (API keys or OAuth client credentials)\n- The [Appwrite Console SDK](/docs/sdks) for Node.js, Python, or another server language\n\n# Step 1: Initialize the Console SDK {% #step-1-initialize-the-console-sdk %}\n\nPartner integrations run on your backend. Initialize the Console SDK with your session or an organization API key:\n\n{% multicode %}\n```server-nodejs\nimport { Client, Organizations, Projects } from 'node-appwrite';\n\nconst client = new Client()\n    .setEndpoint('https://cloud.appwrite.io/v1')\n    .setProject('console');\n\n// With an organization API key (server-to-server)\nclient.setKey(process.env.APPWRITE_ORG_API_KEY);\n\nconst organizations = new Organizations(client);\nconst projects = new Projects(client);\n```\n```server-python\nfrom appwrite.client import Client\nfrom appwrite.services.organizations import Organizations\nfrom appwrite.services.projects import Projects\n\nclient = Client()\nclient.set_endpoint('https://cloud.appwrite.io/v1')\nclient.set_project('console')\nclient.set_key(os.environ['APPWRITE_ORG_API_KEY'])\n\norganizations = Organizations(client)\nprojects = Projects(client)\n```\n{% /multicode %}\n\n{% info title=\"Never expose secrets in client apps\" %}\nOrganization API keys and OAuth client secrets must stay on your server. Use your backend to call Console APIs and project APIs on behalf of users.\n{% /info %}\n\n# Step 2: List or create a project {% #step-2-list-or-create-a-project %}\n\nWith an org API key, list projects in your organization or create one for a new customer:\n\n{% multicode %}\n```server-nodejs\nconst list = await projects.list({\n    queries: [],\n});\n\nconst created = await projects.create({\n    projectId: 'unique()',\n    name: 'Customer workspace',\n    teamId: '<ORGANIZATION_ID>',\n    region: 'fra',\n});\n```\n{% /multicode %}\n\n# Step 3: Manage project resources {% #step-3-manage-project-resources %}\n\nAfter you have a project, use the project SDK with a project API key or dynamic key to manage databases, storage, functions, and other services inside that project. See [Manage resources](/docs/partners/projects/resources).\n\n# Next steps {% #next-steps %}\n\n{% cards %}\n{% cards_item href=\"/docs/partners/oauth-connect/setup\" title=\"Set up OAuth connect\" %}\nRegister an OAuth app and request access to user organizations.\n{% /cards_item %}\n{% cards_item href=\"/docs/partners/org-api-keys/scopes\" title=\"Configure org API key scopes\" %}\nGrant only the Console scopes your platform needs.\n{% /cards_item %}\n{% cards_item href=\"/docs/partners/guides/provisioning\" title=\"Provisioning guide\" %}\nEnd-to-end flow for creating a project per customer.\n{% /cards_item %}\n{% /cards %}\n";
export { quick_start_default as default };
